<title>JAPAN: M'bishi Petroleum to detail Gabon exploring rights.</title>
<headline>M'bishi Petroleum to detail Gabon exploring rights.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-10-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mitsubishi Petroleum Development Co Ltd said it would announce details of its acquisition of exploration rights off the coast of Gabon at 2.30 p.m. (0530 GMT) on Thursday, a company spokeswoman said.</p>
<p>&quot;We can't at the moment say whether it will be oil or gas that we hope to find in the (new) field,&quot; she said.</p>
<p>The company has been producing crude oil in Gabon with France's Elf Aquitaine since 1980. As of November last year, Mitsubishi Development was producing about 13,000 barrels per day.</p>
<p>The company also produces oil in other parts of Africa.</p>
</text>
